    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In a major boost to the quality of education in government schools in Gilgit-Baltistan (GB), the Chief Secretary's Office has launched a capacity building programme for 300 government science teachers. The programme is funded by the Federal Board of Intermediate and Secondary Education Islamabad (FBISE) and is being facilitated by the Aga Khan University-Institute for Educational Development's Professional Development Centre North (AKU-IED PDCN) headed by Dr Mola Dad Shafa.",
